    "role": "user",
    "content": "Program: CBTRN02C. Input files and their record layouts:\n\nDALYTRAN: CVTRA06Y DALYTRAN-RECORD (350 bytes)\n  DALYTRAN-ID                  X(16)\n  DALYTRAN-TYPE-CD             X(2)\n  DALYTRAN-CAT-CD              9(4)\n  DALYTRAN-SOURCE              X(10)\n  DALYTRAN-DESC                X(100)\n  DALYTRAN-AMT                 S9(9)V9(2)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-ID         9(9)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-NAME       X(50)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-CITY       X(50)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-ZIP        X(10)\n  DALYTRAN-CARD-NUM            X(16)\n  DALYTRAN-ORIG-TS             X(26)\n  DALYTRAN-PROC-TS             X(26)\n\nXREF: CVACT03Y CARD-XREF-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  XREF-CARD-NUM                X(16)\n  XREF-CUST-ID                 9(9)\n  XREF-ACCT-ID                 9(11)\n\nACCOUNT: CVACT01Y ACCOUNT-RECORD (300 bytes)\n  ACCT-ID                      9(11)\n  ACCT-ACTIVE-STATUS           X(1)\n  ACCT-CURR-BAL                S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CREDIT-LIMIT            S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CASH-CREDIT-LIMIT       S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-OPEN-DATE               X(10)\n  ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE          X(10)\n  ACCT-REISSUE-DATE            X(10)\n  ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT         S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT          S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-ADDR-ZIP                X(10)\n  ACCT-GROUP-ID                X(10)\n\nTCATBAL: CVTRA01Y TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  TRANCAT-ACCT-ID              9(11)\n  TRANCAT-TYPE-CD              X(2)\n  TRANCAT-CD                   9(4)\n  TRAN-CAT-BAL                 S9(9)V9(2)\n\nRule to test:\n{\n \"id\": \"BR-CBTRN02C-002\",\n \"title\": \"Reject transaction whose cross-referenced account does not exist\",\n \"summary\": \"Once the card is found, the program looks up the account ID from the card cross-reference record in the account file. If no account record exists, the transaction gets reason 101 'ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND' and is rejected. The over-limit and expiration checks do not run.\",\n \"given\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The card cross-reference lookup succeeded, so the fail reason is still 0.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"0\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The account file is read using the account ID from the cross-reference record as the key.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"XREF-ACCT-ID\",\n    \"FD-ACCT-ID\",\n    \"ACCOUNT-RECORD\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  }\n ],\n \"when\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"No account record exists for that account ID (INVALID KEY on the read).\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"ACCOUNT-RECORD\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  }\n ],\n \"then\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The fail reason is set to 101.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"101\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The reason description is set to 'ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND'.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON-DESC\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The credit-limit check (reason 102) and the expiration check (reason 103) are skipped. They only run in the NOT INVALID KEY branch, when the account record is found.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"ACCT-CREDIT-LIMIT\",\n    \"WS-TEMP-BAL\",\n    \"ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"102\",\n    \"103\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The transaction is not posted. The reject count goes up by 1 and a reject record is written.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON\",\n    \"WS-REJECT-COUNT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"0\",\n    \"1\"\n   ]\n  }\n ]\n}"
   }
